Since $k < m < n$, $\frac1k < \frac{19}{84} < \frac3k$, so $\frac{84}{19} < k < \frac{252}{19}$, i.e. $5 \le k \le 13$.

For a fixed $k$, write $\frac{19}{84} - \frac1k = \frac pq$ (lowest terms). Then $\frac1m < \frac pq < \frac2m$ gives $\frac qp < m < \frac{2q}p$, and $n = \frac{1}{p/q - 1/m}$ must be an integer greater than $m$. For example $k = 7$ gives $\frac{19}{84} - \frac17 = \frac1{12}$, so $12 < m < 24$ and $n = \frac{12m}{m - 12}$; $m = 13, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20, 21$ give $n = 156, 84, 60, 48, 36, 30, 28$ — already seven solutions:
$$\{7,13,156\},\ \{7,14,84\},\ \{7,15,60\},\ \{7,16,48\},\ \{7,18,36\},\ \{7,20,30\},\ \{7,21,28\}.$$
Any five of these answer the question.

Doing the same for every $k$ from 5 to 13 gives all **22** solutions:
* $k = 5$: $m = 39, 40, 42, 45, 56, 60, 70$ with $n = 1820, 840, 420, 252, 120, 105, 84$;
* $k = 6$: $m = 17, 18, 20, 21, 24, 28$ with $n = 1428, 252, 105, 84, 56, 42$;
* $k = 7$: the seven above;
* $k = 8$: $(m, n) = (10, 840), (12, 56)$;
* $k = 9, \dots, 13$: none.
